    titre: "Safe SCRIBE memory maintenance commands"
    l0_abstract: "Maintenance commands that can touch SCRIBE state must patch narrowly, validate with doctor, and expose dry-run/report modes."
    pourquoi: "Memory maintenance is higher risk than read-only retrieval: compaction and tier promotion can corrupt long-term agent grounding if they rewrite the YAML wholesale. Targeted text patches plus doctor rollback preserve historical memory while making the SCRIBE operable at scale."
    contexte: "SCRIBE compact/promote/export command design and long-term causal memory operations."
    liens_causaux:
      source: "JOURNAL-024"
