    titre: "Dry-run guarded SCRIBE archival"
    l0_abstract: "SCRIBE archival must default to dry-run, skip active debts, write archive YAML only with `--apply`, and rollback on doctor failure."
    pourquoi: "Archival removes entries from active memory, so it is more dangerous than export; dry-run by default, active-debt skips, archive YAML validation, and doctor rollback make the operation reversible and suitable for long-term memory hygiene."
    contexte: "SCRIBE archive command, cold-tier retention, and active memory pruning."
    liens_causaux:
      source: "JOURNAL-026"
