      - "scribe graph --build: rebuilt bundle graph without vendor/minified god-nodes"
      - "bundle god-nodes: load_scribe, check_all, Finding, write_fixture, ScribeStore"
      - "unittest discover: 18 tests passed"
      - "py_compile: bundle and root shim Python files compiled"
      - "scribe dashboard: generated static HTML and JSON from canonical SCRIBE"
      - "scribe query friciton perfermance: typo query returned friction memory"
      - "scribe doctor: 0 errors, 5 legacy warnings"
    scribe_delta: "PAT-016 | JOURNAL-033"
  - id: "JOURNAL-034"
    date: "2026-05-24"
    mode: "STANDARD"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["VAC-004", "PAT-002", "PAT-012"]
    l0_abstract: "Fixed the Codex PreToolUse hook broken-pipe failure by making Graphify hooks consume stdin."
    pourquoi: "Codex writes a JSON payload to PreToolUse hook stdin; the old silent Graphify command exited immediately, so the runtime hit Broken pipe before the hook could complete. Consuming stdin preserves silent allow behavior while keeping the graphify marker and preventing reinstall from recreating the bad command."
    validations:
      - "project .codex/hooks.json command consumes stdin and exits 0 in a local simulation"
      - "graphify codex install regenerated the stdin-safe hook from the patched template"
      - "both active Graphify Python installations patched in ~/.local and pipx"
      - "scribe doctor: 0 errors, 5 legacy warnings"
    scribe_delta: "VAC-004 | JOURNAL-034"
